SOLUTION
Follow these steps in the Jenkins UI:

Open Jenkins
Click Jenkins on the top bar.
Log in:
Username: admin
Password: Adm!n321
Create user anita
Go to Manage Jenkins → Users.
Click Create User.
Enter:
Username: anita
Password: YchZHRcLkL
Confirm password: YchZHRcLkL
Full name: Anita
Create the user.
Install/enable Matrix Authorization
Go to Manage Jenkins → Plugins → Available plugins.
Search for Matrix Authorization Strategy.
Install it if it isn't already installed.
If prompted, select Restart Jenkins when installation is complete and no jobs are running.
Wait until the Jenkins login page is available again before continuing.
Configure global authorization
Log back in as admin.
Go to Manage Jenkins → Security.
Under Authorization, select:
Project-based Matrix Authorization Strategy.
In the matrix:
Add user: anita
For anita, enable Overall → Read only.
Find Anonymous and ensure every permission is unchecked.
Find admin and ensure Overall → Administer is checked.
Save/Apply.
Configure the existing job
Open the existing Jenkins job.
Click Configure.
Find the Project-based Matrix Authorization Strategy section.
Add anita.
Give anita Job → Read only.
Do not grant Agent, Build, Configure, Delete, Workspace, SCM, or any other permissions.
Save.
Verify
Log out of admin.
Log in as:
Username: anita
Password: YchZHRcLkL
Confirm anita can see/read the existing job but cannot configure, build, delete, or otherwise administer it.
Log back in as admin and confirm Overall → Administer remains enabled.

For the screenshots, capture at least the global authorization matrix and the job-level matrix, showing anita, Anonymous, and admin permissions.
